<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
    "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for corevideo-zoom-engine.app, the process that links the Zoom
  Meeting SDK. Ported from the CoreVideo OBS plugin recipe. Only the engine
  carries these; the shell and core do not load the Zoom SDK.

  NOTE ON STYLE: no double hyphens anywhere in this comment. XML forbids them
  inside comments and Apple's AMFIUnserializeXML enforces that strictly, so a
  double hyphen fails every codesign call with a bare syntax error.

  disable-library-validation is LOAD BEARING. ZoomSDK.framework is not self
  contained: at auth it loads sibling BUNDLES (ssb_sdk, zNet, zPTUIEx and
  others) through the MAIN BUNDLE Contents/Frameworks directory, not via rpath.
  Hardened runtime turns library validation on and that load is refused. The
  failure is sdkAuth returning Failed(1) synchronously with no delegate
  callback, and it only shows up once the build is signed with the runtime.

  The camera and audio-input entitlements are for the SDK own UI (camera
  picker, meeting audio). TCC still needs the usage description strings in the
  engine Info.plist, which make-macos-engine-bundle.sh writes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
